<title>UK: Colombia may rewrite some oil contracts - minister.</title>
<headline>Colombia may rewrite some oil contracts - minister.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombia's Mines and Energy Minister said on Monday he was considering cutting the government share of profits on some oil exploration contracts to encourage more foreign investment in the petroleum sector.</p>
<p>Rodrigo Villamizar said Colombia's so-called &quot;sliding-scale&quot; contracts, used by British Petroleum Co Plc in the Piedemonte development, were too harsh on foreign producers, especially when they discovered natural gas.</p>
</text>
